IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-nouns`
IMPORT `g2-readings`
IMPORT `g2-art5-charity-test`
IMPORT `g2-art6-purposes`
IMPORT `g2-art7-public-benefit`

-- ind-b-tests-fixtures-g2: the fixtures of test author ind-b for Articles 5 to 7 (group G2).  No assertions: the facts here are the scenarios of
-- work/ind-b/expectations.md, put into the shapes of the G2 modules.

§ `ind-b fixtures for Articles 5 to 7`

GIVEN p IS A TYPE
      a IS A TYPE
      d IS A DEONTIC p a
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-b nothing is owed under` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`ind-b no Article 6 facts` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
        `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE
        `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE
        `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose promotes equality` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose promotes diversity` IS NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A STRING
      h IS A MAYBE `Head of charitable purpose`
GIVETH A Purpose
`ind-b purpose` d h MEANS
    Purpose WITH
        description IS d
        head IS h
        `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE
        `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE
        `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

GIVEN d IS A STRING
GIVETH A Purpose
`ind-b ancillary purpose` d MEANS
    Purpose WITH
        description IS d
        head IS NOTHING
        `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS TRUE
        `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE
        `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

GIVEN d IS A STRING
      h IS A MAYBE `Head of charitable purpose`
      anc IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Purpose
`ind-b political purpose` d h anc MEANS
    Purpose WITH
        description IS d
        head IS h
        `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS anc
        `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS TRUE
        `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

GIVEN p IS A Purpose
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`ind-b with no facts` p MEANS
    `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` WITH
        purpose IS p
        facts IS `ind-b no Article 6 facts`

GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      pfs IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
GIVETH AN Entity
`ind-b entity` standing pfs MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS "the test entity"
        `standing on the register` IS standing
        `kinds of entity` IS LIST `a company`
        `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
        governors IS EMPTY
        purposes IS map (GIVEN pf YIELD pf's purpose) pfs

-- A determination by `who`, finding (or not) that the entity provides, or intends to provide, public benefit; its maker did everything the Law requires of it.
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
      provides IS A BOOLEAN
      intends IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`ind-b determination by` who provides intends MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS who
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS provides
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS intends
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

-- The same, but the entity benefits only identified natural persons (Article 7(3)(b)); the maker did not treat them as a section of the public.
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
      provides IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`ind-b determination of an entity benefiting only identified persons, by` who provides MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS who
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS provides
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS TRUE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

-- A determination by the Commissioner that presumed the purpose to be for the public benefit (Article 7(3)(a)) and so found public benefit.
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`ind-b determination that presumed public benefit` MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS `the Commissioner`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS TRUE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

-- A determination by the Commissioner where benefit goes to a section of the public only, under a fee the Commissioner had regard to (Article 7(2)(b)).
GIVEN provides IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`ind-b determination of a fee-charging section of the public, finding` provides MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS `the Commissioner`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS provides
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`ind-b a constitution that permits nothing of Article 5(2)` MEANS
    `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` WITH `permissions that the constitution expressly makes` IS EMPTY

GIVEN what IS A `What a constitution expressly permits`
      who IS A `Person named in Article 5(2)`
      capacity IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`ind-b a constitution permitting` what who capacity MEANS
    `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` WITH
        `permissions that the constitution expressly makes` IS LIST (`Permission that a constitution expressly makes` WITH
                                                                        `what the constitution expressly permits` IS what
                                                                        `the person permitted` IS who
                                                                        `acting in that capacity` IS capacity)

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      pfs IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
      constitution IS A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
      determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
      order IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-b charity test` interp standing pfs constitution determination order MEANS
    `Art 5 the entity meets the charity test` interp (`ind-b entity` standing pfs) pfs constitution `the Chief Minister` determination order

`ind-b A` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
`ind-b education` MEANS `ind-b with no facts` (`ind-b purpose` "the advancement of education" (JUST `the advancement of education`))
`ind-b poverty` MEANS `ind-b with no facts` (`ind-b purpose` "the relief of poverty" (JUST `the prevention or relief of poverty`))
`ind-b shop` MEANS `ind-b with no facts` (`ind-b ancillary purpose` "running a shop to raise funds for the charitable purpose")
`ind-b profit` MEANS `ind-b with no facts` (`ind-b purpose` "making profits for the members" NOTHING)
`ind-b candidate` MEANS `ind-b with no facts` (`ind-b political purpose` "promoting a candidate for election" NOTHING TRUE)
`ind-b none` MEANS `ind-b a constitution that permits nothing of Article 5(2)`
`ind-b PB by the Commissioner` MEANS `ind-b determination by` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE
`ind-b no PB by the Commissioner` MEANS `ind-b determination by` `the Commissioner` FALSE FALSE
`ind-b intended PB by the Commissioner` MEANS `ind-b determination by` `the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE
GIVETH A `Standing on the register`
`ind-b general` MEANS `entered in the general section`
GIVETH A `Standing on the register`
`ind-b applicant` MEANS `an applicant for registration`

§ `ind-b fixtures for Article 6`

GIVEN h IS A `Head of charitable purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-b the head alone is charitable` h MEANS
    `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "a purpose" (JUST h)) `ind-b no Article 6 facts`

GIVEN sport IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`ind-b sport facts` sport MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
        `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE
        `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE
        `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS sport
        `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose promotes equality` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose promotes diversity` IS NOTHING

GIVEN need IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      public IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`ind-b recreation facts` need public MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
        `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE
        `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE
        `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS need
        `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS public
        `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose promotes equality` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose promotes diversity` IS NOTHING

GIVEN sickness IS A BOOLEAN
      regeneration IS A BOOLEAN
      civic IS A BOOLEAN
      accommodation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`ind-b clarification facts` sickness regeneration civic accommodation MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
        `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE
        `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS sickness
        `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS regeneration
        `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS civic
        `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS accommodation
        `the purpose promotes equality` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose promotes diversity` IS NOTHING

`ind-b equality and diversity facts` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
        `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE
        `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE
        `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose promotes equality` IS JUST TRUE
        `the purpose promotes diversity` IS JUST TRUE



-- (added by the integrator) the facts of `ind-b recreation facts` with the object of improving the conditions of life stated FALSE: row E6-2d4 is recreational facilities available to the public WITHOUT that object.
GIVEN need IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      public IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`ind-b recreation facts without the object` need public MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
        `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST FALSE
        `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE
        `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS need
        `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS public
        `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose promotes equality` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose promotes diversity` IS NOTHING